      "writtenOn": "2022-02-22T21:12:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "These files can still be analyzed in a run without timeouts, they just take longer than 90 seconds. At some point, we will have clang-tidy lints even for files that take \u003e 90s to analyze in gerrit. `tidy_disabled_srcs` is for files that might exhibit current crashes with clang-tidy, or have some other properties that make them unsuitable for ever analyzing. `tidy_timeout_srcs` is something that we\u0027ll take care of for now, since it is mostly related to ensuring that our daily reports don\u0027t become flaky (due to borderline timeouts causing diagnostics to appear/disappear on different days).",
